on":[{"@type":"OpeningHoursSpecification","dayOfWeek":["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday"],"opens":"08:00","closes":"18:00"}],"priceRange":"$$"},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/#website","url":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/","name":"Arkansas Insurance Appraiser","publisher":{"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/#webpage","url":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/","name":"Insurance Appraisal Process Explained | 8 Steps","description":"The insurance appraisal process explained for Arkansas policyholders: the written demand, naming appraisers, the umpire and the binding award.","inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/#website"},"about":{"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"dateModified":"2026-11-13","primaryImageOfPage":{"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/#primaryimage"},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/#breadcrumb"},"mainEntity":{"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/#howto"}},{"@type":"ImageObject","@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/#primaryimage","url":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/planner.webp","contentUrl":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/planner.webp","width":1024,"height":684,"caption":"Notebook, coffee cup and phone on a table during a planning session"},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Appraisal process","item":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/"}],"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/#breadcrumb"},{"@type":"HowTo","name":"How the insurance appraisal process works in Arkansas","description":"The stages of a property insurance appraisal, from the disagreement to the signed award.","step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"Pin down the disagreement","text":"Confirm the carrier has accepted coverage and that the dispute is about the amount of loss, not whether the loss is covered.","url":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/#step-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"Read the appraisal paragraph","text":"Find the appraisal condition in your policy and note its deadlines, how the umpire is chosen and how costs are split.","url":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/#step-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"Send a written demand","text":"Either side can demand appraisal in writing. The letter identifies the claim and the items in dispute.","url":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/#step-3"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Name the appraisers","text":"Each side names a competent, impartial appraiser, usually within about 20 days of the demand.","url":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/#step-4"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":5,"name":"Select an umpire","text":"The two appraisers try to agree on an umpire. If they can’t, either side can usually ask a court to appoint one.","url":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/#step-5"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":6,"name":"Appraisers compare estimates","text":"The appraisers inspect, exchange estimates and work through the differences line by line.","url":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/#step-6"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":7,"name":"Umpire decides what’s left","text":"Items the appraisers can’t settle go to the umpire with photos, measurements and pricing support.","url":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/#step-7"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":8,"name":"Award is signed and paid","text":"An award signed by any two of the three sets the amount of loss. Payment follows under the policy’s terms.","url":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/#step-8"}],"@id":"https://arkansasinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-process-explained/#howto"}]}</script>
